{"title":"Career Roadmap · HVAC Engineer","role":"HVAC Engineer","summary":"An HVAC Engineer designs, analyses, installs, commissions and maintains Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning systems. The role combines thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, heat transfer, refrigeration, building services, controls and energy efficiency.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build thermal engineering, HVAC design, CAD/BIM and site-engineering fundamentals"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in HVAC design, MEP coordination, commissioning or energy management"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Move toward senior HVAC design, project management, energy optimisation or building-services leadership"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine HVAC with smart buildings, heat pumps, building automation, renewable energy and low-carbon design"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Mechanical Engineering → HVAC Engineer","text":"Direct alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"Mechanical Engineering provides the core foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Refrigeration and air conditioning"},{"text":"Engineering mechanics"},{"text":"Machine design"},{"text":"Thermal engineering"},{"text":"Building services"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should additionally develop HVAC load calculations, duct design, piping, equipment selection, BIM/CAD, HVAC controls, commissioning and energy analysis."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Long-range horizons are planning guidance; exact market requirements should be verified."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[